{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KpwY6NCL6vmCeZ8LkR7MEt","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t`calibration.md` is written and updated. Here's a summary of what it contains:\n2\t\n3\t---\n4\t\n5\t## What's in calibration.md\n6\t\n7\t**Benchmark identity**: Single Lean 4 existence proof (`∃ n, n ∉ setAB`), NOT a neural benchmark race. Score = 1.0 iff clean compile with zero `sorry`.\n8\t\n9\t**Current SOTA** (with numbers):\n10\t- Seed-Prover (ByteDance, Jul 2025): **100%** on MiniF2F — fully saturated\n11\t- Goedel-Prover-V2-32B: **90.4%** pass@32 (self-correction mode)\n12\t- DeepSeek-Prover-V2-671B: **88.9%** pass@8192, recursive subgoal decomposition + RL\n13\t- Kimina-Prover: **80.7%** pass@8192, structured reasoning + RL\n14\t- HyperTree Proof Search: **41.0%** test (AlphaZero MCTS, now far behind)\n15\t\n16\t**The witness**: **n = 62** is the smallest natural not in setAB.\n17\t\n18\t- **b-side proof** (8 cases): setB ∩ [0,62] = {0,1,4,5,16,17,20,21}. For each b, a=62−b has a base-3 digit of 2 (e.g., 62−16=46=\"1201\"₃).\n19\t- **a-side proof** (16 cases): setA ∩ [0,62] = {0,1,3,4,9,10,12,13,27,28,30,31,36,37,39,40}. For each a, b=62−a has a base-4 digit ≥ 2.\n20\t- **Modular shortcut** (6 cases): `b%4 ∈ {0,1}` + `62%4=2` → `a%4 ∈ {1,2}`, leaving only {1,9,13,37,10,30} to check.\n21\t\n22\t**Recommended proof order**: `native_decide` → `decide` → `interval_cases b` (bounded) → explicit 8-case split → modular shortcut (Option E).\n23\t\n24\t**Key failure modes documented**: don't `decide` the unbounded existential (loops), don't use n < 62 (they're all in setAB), don't use `omega`/`linarith` for digit goals.\n25\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0dc3adb-0c97-4603-b717-1a14a092c988","uuid":"85b6b2dd-6c31-4b98-b38f-8af95a13daaa","timestamp":"2026-05-26T22:46:53.527Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/vincent/researchRalph/domains/erdos-125-claudeception/calibration.md","content":"`calibration.md` is written and updated. Here's a summary of what it contains:\n\n---\n\n## What's in calibration.md\n\n**Benchmark identity**: Single Lean 4 existence proof (`∃ n, n ∉ setAB`), NOT a neural benchmark race. Score = 1.0 iff clean compile with zero `sorry`.\n\n**Current SOTA** (with numbers):\n- Seed-Prover (ByteDance, Jul 2025): **100%** on MiniF2F — fully saturated\n- Goedel-Prover-V2-32B: **90.4%** pass@32 (self-correction mode)\n- DeepSeek-Prover-V2-671B: **88.9%** pass@8192, recursive subgoal decomposition + RL\n- Kimina-Prover: **80.7%** pass@8192, structured reasoning + RL\n- HyperTree Proof Search: **41.0%** test (AlphaZero MCTS, now far behind)\n\n**The witness**: **n = 62** is the smallest natural not in setAB.\n\n- **b-side proof** (8 cases): setB ∩ [0,62] = {0,1,4,5,16,17,20,21}. For each b, a=62−b has a base-3 digit of 2 (e.g., 62−16=46=\"1201\"₃).\n- **a-side proof** (16 cases): setA ∩ [0,62] = {0,1,3,4,9,10,12,13,27,28,30,31,36,37,39,40}. For each a, b=62−a has a base-4 digit ≥ 2.\n- **Modular shortcut** (6 cases): `b%4 ∈ {0,1}` + `62%4=2` → `a%4 ∈ {1,2}`, leaving only {1,9,13,37,10,30} to check.\n\n**Recommended proof order**: `native_decide` → `decide` → `interval_cases b` (bounded) → explicit 8-case split → modular shortcut (Option E).\n\n**Key failure modes documented**: don't `decide` the unbounded existential (loops), don't use n < 62 (they're all in setAB), don't use `omega`/`linarith` for digit goals.\n","numLines":25,"startLine":1,"totalLines":25}}}
